      "valuation_insights": "### Valuation Insights for Costco Wholesale Corporation (COST)\n\nCostco's fiscal year 2026 total revenue was $303.15 billion [C:revenue] with robust year-over-year growth of 10.1% [C:revenue_growth], indicating sustained topline expansion. The company generated operating income of $11.685 billion [C:operating_income], yielding an operating margin of 3.85% [C:operating_margin], which, while positive, remains slightly below Walmart's 4.18% [C:wmt_operating_margin] and Target's 4.88% [C:tgt_operating_margin], reflecting Costco's competitive cost structure in the wholesale sector. Net income attributable to Costco was $9.226 billion [C:net_income], translating to a GAAP diluted EPS of $20.76 [C:diluted_eps].\n\nReturn on average equity stood at a high 28.4% [C:return_on_average_equity], demonstrating efficient capital utilization. The debt-to-equity ratio, including the current portion of long-term debt, was a modest 0.17 [C:debt_to_equity], underscoring a conservative leverage profile, especially when compared to peers. Free cash flow was strong at $9.382 billion [C:free_cash_flow], providing capacity for strategic investments or returns to shareholders.\n\nFrom the latest quarterly earnings, net sales increased 11.2% year-over-year to $93.9 billion [C:q4_revenue], with a diluted EPS of $6.75 [C:q4_diluted_eps]. Based on a recent share price of $904.7, Costco trades at a P/E multiple of 43.58 [C:price_to_earnings], reflecting market expectations for continued growth and profitability.\n\nCostco's focus on international expansion and digitally-enabled sales, noted in the release [L:10], may sustain topline momentum. The lower operating margin relative to peers could be a function of membership-driven pricing or cost absorption strategies, which warrants monitoring.\n\nInsight: Costco’s reduced long-term debt level from $5.71 billion last year to $3.91 billion this year while increasing operating income suggests effective debt management paired with operational efficiency (10-K line 85) [L:10-K].",
